MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Piano Guys feels like a natural next choice after my relaxing classical album because instrumental crossover suits the calm listening I want now.",
    "Partners and Cheek to Cheek connect with my interest in polished vocals and musical standards, which also draws me to theatrical and crossover recordings."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me connects with my past Christmas listening, but enjoying holiday music sometimes does not mean I want it today.",
    "In The Lonely Hour does not offer the orchestral or crossover sound I currently prefer, while Platinum feels too far from today's quieter mood."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My occasional country listening seems to have been treated as a stronger current preference than it is; Tornado interests me, but it is not what I want now.",
    "Expressive singing alone is not enough to make an album my next choice. Loved Me Back to Life has vocal appeal, but today I would choose quieter instrumental music."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent relaxing classical selection matters more to today's choice than some of my older listening interests.",
    "Interest does not always mean readiness to choose: I would preview Hope and check the tracks on Nostalgia before committing, whereas The Piano Guys feels like an immediate fit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my taste for polished vocals and crossover music but give too little weight to my current preference for calm instrumental listening."
}
